# WIP: Urgent Necropsy; intentionally not an applicable fix.
# Diagnosis: Oracle defines the additional Collect Evidence amount as the
# total mana value of this spell's chosen permanent targets. The parser currently
# stores CollectEvidence.amount as u32, and the additional-cost parser does not
# bind a trailing where-X quantity to that cost. The existing where-X cost
# rebinder also treats CollectEvidence as a fixed-cost no-op.
#
# The quantity side is representable: PropertyAggregate can sum ObjectManaValue
# over CardTypeSetSource::TargetedObjects { slot: None }. The missing seam is
# carrying that dynamic expression through the shared casting-cost path. A
# complete fix must preserve legacy serialized fixed amounts, defer target-
# dependent payability until targets are chosen, resolve the amount from the
# pending cast's targets before collect-evidence payment, and keep activation
# cost consumers correct. Relevant paths include AbilityCost::CollectEvidence,
# parse_additional_cost_line / parse_single_cost, cost_payability,
# casting_costs, and collect_evidence::begin_cost_payment.
#
# Verified rules: CR 107.3c (text-defined X), CR 202.3 (mana value),
# CR 601.2c and 601.2h (targets precede total-cost payment), and CR 701.59a
# (collect evidence). Static Collect Evidence on Detective's Phoenix /
# Conspiracy Unraveler and dynamic PayLife cost binding are analogues, but neither
# covers a target-derived Collect Evidence threshold.
#
# No parser or engine files were changed and no runtime test was run. This is a
# shared AST/casting-payment seam rather than a parser-local fix; park pending
# a general dynamic cost-amount design and a scenario test with multiple targets
# whose mana values must be summed.
